      "message": "I\u0027m adding Wayland window surface support to ANGLE\u0027s WGPU backend (cr bug: angle/7885810). Currently build_overrides/dawn.gni can\u0027t set dawn_use_wayland because declare_args() blocks overrides from imported files when the values differ. This change switches to if (!defined()) guards, consistent with how dawn_overrides_with_defaults.gni handles every other config variable.\n\nAlso changed the default from false to is_linux \u0026\u0026 !is_chromeos so that standalone Linux builds get both X11 and Wayland surface support by default, matching dawn_use_x11.\n\nCould I also get CQ dryrun access? I\u0027d like to be able to trigger trybots for future Dawn changes related to ANGLE integration.",
